[[:db/retract 17592186162392 :question/answer-fields 17592186159554] [:db/retract 17592186162396 :question/answer-fields 17592186159578] {:db/id 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6fd86b7a-aa64-5ea3-a90b-7af5da2353f8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162392 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}24xy, & \\,0<x<1,0<y<1-x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1-x}24xy\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24x{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24x{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1-x} \\\\  & =12x(1-x)^{2}-0 \\\\  & =12x(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)={\\begin{aligned}12x(x-1)^{2}, & \\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal density function for $X.$\n\nNow, for $0<x<1,0<y<1-x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{24xy}{12x(x-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{(x-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{(x-1)^{2}}, & \\,0<x<1,0<y<1-x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}) & =P(Y<\\frac{1}{3}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x=\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2y}{{(\\frac{1}{3}-1)}^{2}}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\frac{1}{18}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7133b6f3-994d-586b-8bc7-52facdb8edd3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7133b6f3-994d-586b-8bc7-52facdb8edd3" :answer-field/id #uuid "7133b6f3-994d-586b-8bc7-52facdb8edd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76dedc47-c082-5f11-bb91-f5c53a5feef0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db303bfa-69cf-5cf1-86a5-b4a2624334a1" "answer-76dedc47-c082-5f11-bb91-f5c53a5feef0" "answer-efd7c23f-d7a0-5417-baaf-c56cd1849f93" "answer-fcf61311-9fef-553a-a566-6bcfee2063e1" "answer-b6e703b0-4bd0-5a40-af83-db0c989a5aba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db303bfa-69cf-5cf1-86a5-b4a2624334a1" :answer/id #uuid "db303bfa-69cf-5cf1-86a5-b4a2624334a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76dedc47-c082-5f11-bb91-f5c53a5feef0" :answer/id #uuid "76dedc47-c082-5f11-bb91-f5c53a5feef0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efd7c23f-d7a0-5417-baaf-c56cd1849f93" :answer/id #uuid "efd7c23f-d7a0-5417-baaf-c56cd1849f93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcf61311-9fef-553a-a566-6bcfee2063e1" :answer/id #uuid "fcf61311-9fef-553a-a566-6bcfee2063e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6e703b0-4bd0-5a40-af83-db0c989a5aba" :answer/id #uuid "b6e703b0-4bd0-5a40-af83-db0c989a5aba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6fd86b7a-aa64-5ea3-a90b-7af5da2353f8" :question/id #uuid "6fd86b7a-aa64-5ea3-a90b-7af5da2353f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-143574" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}8xy, & \\,0\\le x\\le y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<\\frac{1}{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{2}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}8xy\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8y{\\int }_{0}^{y}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8y{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{y} \\\\  & =4y({y}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =4{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)={\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{3}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8xy}{4{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}, & \\,0\\le x\\le y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<\\frac{1}{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{2}{3}) & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{2}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}\\frac{2x}{{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}{\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}{[{x}^{2}]}_{1/4}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{3}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76914fbd-7e46-5e1e-a2ea-82b62a7c5f3c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76914fbd-7e46-5e1e-a2ea-82b62a7c5f3c" :answer-field/id #uuid "76914fbd-7e46-5e1e-a2ea-82b62a7c5f3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0d7ebaa8-7f99-5427-8a2f-237d9f6e4410" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0232ff5b-0d05-5778-88a0-ff0af66fc111" "answer-0d7ebaa8-7f99-5427-8a2f-237d9f6e4410" "answer-cb999cce-827d-57cd-aed2-f09c922819e1" "answer-2bab8694-81fe-5f61-ab63-c2f3224466f2" "answer-291ffaa1-af34-572c-8208-632d599387b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0232ff5b-0d05-5778-88a0-ff0af66fc111" :answer/id #uuid "0232ff5b-0d05-5778-88a0-ff0af66fc111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d7ebaa8-7f99-5427-8a2f-237d9f6e4410" :answer/id #uuid "0d7ebaa8-7f99-5427-8a2f-237d9f6e4410" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb999cce-827d-57cd-aed2-f09c922819e1" :answer/id #uuid "cb999cce-827d-57cd-aed2-f09c922819e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bab8694-81fe-5f61-ab63-c2f3224466f2" :answer/id #uuid "2bab8694-81fe-5f61-ab63-c2f3224466f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-291ffaa1-af34-572c-8208-632d599387b4" :answer/id #uuid "291ffaa1-af34-572c-8208-632d599387b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162396 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{4xy}{5}+\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{5}+\\frac{6x{y}^{2}}{5}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8y}{5}+\\frac{12{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{2y}{5}-\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{6y}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2y(2x+3y)}{5})}{(\\frac{6y(y+1)}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+3y}{3(y+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3y}{3(y+1)}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2b4844fd-48c8-5187-86c9-fcbf91d0bc32"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2b4844fd-48c8-5187-86c9-fcbf91d0bc32" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b4844fd-48c8-5187-86c9-fcbf91d0bc32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2b4b973f-cb9d-5e7e-8beb-4c556f2b875c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e77674d9-5e17-517e-8f5b-956421030e91" "answer-6a95ee3c-3035-5909-a68e-b2eac9893340" "answer-726964d4-b990-596e-9009-e83d6d208a25" "answer-b7e4876d-bca4-5991-b345-bf1e1f8f35e9" "answer-2b4b973f-cb9d-5e7e-8beb-4c556f2b875c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e77674d9-5e17-517e-8f5b-956421030e91" :answer/id #uuid "e77674d9-5e17-517e-8f5b-956421030e91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+3y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a95ee3c-3035-5909-a68e-b2eac9893340" :answer/id #uuid "6a95ee3c-3035-5909-a68e-b2eac9893340" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5y(x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-726964d4-b990-596e-9009-e83d6d208a25" :answer/id #uuid "726964d4-b990-596e-9009-e83d6d208a25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+3y)(y+1)}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7e4876d-bca4-5991-b345-bf1e1f8f35e9" :answer/id #uuid "b7e4876d-bca4-5991-b345-bf1e1f8f35e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(y+1)}{5(2x+3y)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b4b973f-cb9d-5e7e-8beb-4c556f2b875c" :answer/id #uuid "2b4b973f-cb9d-5e7e-8beb-4c556f2b875c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+3y}{3(y+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-8d71dbb8-3f6b-51a3-b4b2-a5b2c8b23a9b" :activity/id #uuid "8d71dbb8-3f6b-51a3-b4b2-a5b2c8b23a9b" :activity/title "Conditional Distributions for Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050535 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-cd604f93-e377-5bb5-97aa-db0cfd4f422a" "step-9476e3d9-7d05-54ea-ba2e-44132f1512b5" "step-a4e2ce8c-ef99-5939-91ca-5637d283ed7e"] :activity/first-step "step-cd604f93-e377-5bb5-97aa-db0cfd4f422a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-cd604f93-e377-5bb5-97aa-db0cfd4f422a" :step/id #uuid "cd604f93-e377-5bb5-97aa-db0cfd4f422a" :step/content 17592186162392 :step/next "step-9476e3d9-7d05-54ea-ba2e-44132f1512b5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9476e3d9-7d05-54ea-ba2e-44132f1512b5" :step/id #uuid "9476e3d9-7d05-54ea-ba2e-44132f1512b5" :step/content "question-6fd86b7a-aa64-5ea3-a90b-7af5da2353f8" :step/next "step-a4e2ce8c-ef99-5939-91ca-5637d283ed7e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a4e2ce8c-ef99-5939-91ca-5637d283ed7e" :step/id #uuid "a4e2ce8c-ef99-5939-91ca-5637d283ed7e" :step/content 17592186162396 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
